.TH CUTTING-GARDEN-CAPTURE 1
.SH NAME
cutting-garden-capture - capture one or more directory trees into madder's blob stores
.SH DESCRIPTION
Walks each source path (or hands URL-shaped args to the matching plugin), writes every regular file as a content-addressed blob, and emits one receipt blob per store group describing the captured entries.
.PP
Partial results are deliberately durable. Per-entry failures and interruption (SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP) do not discard completed work: every entry captured before the abort is still folded into the store-group receipt, the receipt blob is written, and captures.log records it. The run itself reports the failure \(em failing phase records and a bailout on the event stream, and a nonzero exit \(em but the receipt blob carries no interrupted marker: it is an ordinary receipt describing exactly the entries that were captured. Blobs are content-addressed, so re-running the same capture after an interruption re-reads the sources but stores nothing twice.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B args
interleaved sequence of optional store-ids (starting with `.`) and one or more source paths. Bare paths capture into the default store; a store-id token retargets every path that follows until the next store-id (FDR 0001 §Producer Rules §Group Resolution). Plugins accept URL-shaped paths too (e.g. `ytdlp:https://…`).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Root for the per-capture audit log `$XDG_STATE_HOME/cutting-garden/captures.log` (one NDJSON entry per receipt, best-effort — capture succeeds even if the path is unwritable).
Default: $HOME/.local/state
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cutting-garden/captures.log
NDJSON audit log of every written receipt — including partial receipts from failed or interrupted runs. Best-effort write.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/madder/<store>/
Default blob-store root. Captured entries and receipt blobs land here under their content-addressed paths.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Capture a single tree into the default store (tap-ndjson records when piped).
.B cutting-garden capture src
.TP
Capture into a non-default store; the leading dot disambiguates store-id from path.
.B cutting-garden capture .work src
.TP
Multi-root capture across two stores in one invocation.
.B cutting-garden capture .default src .work docs
.TP
TAP-14 output for CI consumers (phases as test points, entries as subtests).
.B cutting-garden capture -format tap src
.TP
The pre-unification wire (DEPRECATED; dual-format window only).
.B cutting-garden capture -format json-legacy src
.TP
Capture a URL-shaped argument via a registered plugin (e.g. yt-dlp).
.B cutting-garden capture 'ytdlp:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=…'
.SH SEE ALSO
cutting-garden(1), cutting-garden-restore(1), cutting-garden-diff(1), yt-dlp(1)
